  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 258 AM CST Mon Nov 16 2026\n\nThe compact closed low that brought light rain to the area Sun \nmorning is now tracking down across the Arklatex region. Meanwhile, \nweak upper ridging is situated over the Southern/Central Rockies. At \nthe surface, large area of high pressure spans from the Ozark region \nthrough the Ohio and Tennessee Valleys. \n\nThe main forecast challenge for today will be how quickly low clouds \ndissipate across the western half of the forecast area, as this\nwill have an impact on temps. Low clouds currently blanket \nareas generally along and west of I-135 and current thinking is \nthat they will remain through at least the early afternoon hours \nand possibly longer. So will go a bit cooler for highs today \nalong our western flank. \n\nLate tonight, our next shortwave trough will be coming on shore over \ncentral/southern CA and will be moving into the Great Basin by Tue \nevening. This impulse is then expected to lift across the \ncentral/Northern Plains on Wed/Wed evening. Keeping with the \nthinking that gusty south/southwest winds will be the main impact \nthis wave will have on our area. While wind speeds will be \nhigher than they have been over the last several days, they are \nnot expected to be too extreme. The higher gusts for both Tue \nand Wed will be around 40 mph with sustained speeds in the 25 to\n30 mph range. For Tue afternoon the higher wind speeds will be \nwest of I-135 and on Wed will be across south central KS into \nthe Flint Hills. \n\nPattern will remain very progressive with another shortwave trough \nexpected to take a very similar path to the Tue-Wed system. This late \nweek trough will be passing over the Rockies on Fri and out across \nthe Central Plains on Fri night through Sat. Along with gusty south \nwinds on Fri, this impulse will bring some rainfall chances for Fri \nnight through Sat. The progressive nature of the trough will keep \nany mention of heavy rain out of the forecast. \n\nStill looking for a warming trend through the work week with highs \ntoday expected to be the coolest through the next several days. By \nWed, most of the area will have highs in the 60s, with upper 60s to \naround 70 likely for both Thu and Fri.",
